Retail Sales Performance Dashboard

This project explores retail transaction data to understand sales performance, customer behaviour, and product trends. The goal was to transform raw transactional data into meaningful business insights using SQL and Power BI.

The process began with preparing the dataset using SQL. The raw retail data was cleaned and structured to make it suitable for analysis. SQL was used to filter invalid records, calculate revenue from quantity and unit price, and create aggregated tables for customers, products, and monthly revenue trends.

Once the data was prepared, it was imported into Power BI where additional analysis was performed using DAX measures. Key metrics such as total revenue, total orders, total customers, and average order value were calculated to support the dashboard.

The final dashboard is structured into multiple analytical sections including an executive overview, customer insights, product performance, and sales analysis. These dashboards help highlight revenue trends over time, identify top-performing products and customers, and reveal how sales are distributed across different markets.

This project demonstrates how SQL data preparation combined with Power BI visualisation can transform raw data into actionable business intelligence.
